{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And the one afflicted with tzara'at, in whom the plague is, etc.</b> What does the verse teach by saying 'in whom the plague is'? It is obvious — for if there is no plague in him, he is not afflicted with tzara'at. From here there is proof that 'tzara'at' is the name of the affliction, as explained above, and so will be explained further in the nearby portion of Metzora; and 'plague' (נֶגַע) is an epithet for sin, for the sinner touches (נוֹגֵעַ) the honor of Heaven or the honor of creatures. And this is the view of the Midrash that says: 'כְּנֶגַע נִרְאָה לִי בַּבַּיִת' — this is idolatry, etc. (Yalkut Shimoni, Metzora 14, §563). Therefore it says here concerning the one afflicted with tzara'at, who was stricken with tzara'at for speaking evil tongue to defame creatures — and the statement of the Sages, blessed be their memory, that whoever disqualifies with his own blemish disqualifies (Kiddushin 70a) — therefore it is written 'in whom the plague is,' for in him is found, in essence and first of all, every plague and disgrace that he wished to inflict upon his fellow. 'His head shall be disheveled' — to atone for his arrogance, for he wished to be at the head (לְרֹאשׁ) over every person. 'And his garments shall be torn' — to atone for narrowness of eye, for every narrow-eyed person presumably also has his garments torn and patched. 'And he shall cover his upper lip' — to atone for the sin of the tongue that is on his lips. 'And he shall call out: Tamei, tamei!' — for he who defiles others with the produce of his lips, then 'tamei' shall he too be called, for one who disqualifies is himself disqualified. And 'all the days that the plague is in him' — that is, the sin — then 'he shall be tamei,' because 'he is tamei' from the side of his deeds."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:25.985776036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}